  "content": "# Investigation Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (from Phase 1 discovery):**\n\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Course catalog subject offering table: one row per subject offering per term/academic year. Carries `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `SUBJECT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_NUMBER`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SUBJECT_ID`, and links to terms via both `TERM_CODE` (offering term) and `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` (term from which catalog attributes take effect).\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Academic term dimension: one row per term with `TERM_CODE`, `TERM_DESCRIPTION`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, `TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR`, etc.\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY** — Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, and detailed enrollment statistics.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Textbook Information Program subject offered table: one row per subject per term in the textbook program scope, with `SUBJECT_ID`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, and `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL` flag. Parent of TIP_DETAIL.\n- **TIP_DETAIL** — TIP detail table linking subjects offered per term to their textbook materials: `SUBJECT_ID`, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` ('RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'NM' = no materials, etc.), `TIP_MATERIAL_KEY`, `ISBN`, `RECORD_COUNT`. Granularity: one row per subject-material-status combination per term.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered per term with `SUBJECT_ID`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, enrollment numbers.\n- **TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS** — Lookup decoding TIP material status keys ('RQ' = Required, etc.); key equals code.\n\n**Column concepts:**\n\n- **column_concept_total_units** — TOTAL_UNITS replicated across COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (catalog-declared), SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (registrar subject-l