COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS (EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE) ⋈ SUBJECT_SUMMARY (TERM_CODE) with `RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY SUBJECT_CODE)`.\n- Department stats over TIP-required-material subjects: 1 direct precedent — dw_4724's Sub2 CTE: `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ TIP_DETAIL ON SUBJECT_ID ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY ON SUBJECT_ID WHERE TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY='RQ' GROUP BY OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (there with COUNT/MIN; here AVG/range/VARIANCE per hint mapping).\n- \"at least one enrolled student\" on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: dw_1350 (`>= 1`), dw_1954/dw_3644 (`> 0` / `>= 1` variants).\n- Range = `MAX(...) - MIN(...)`: dw_3311, dw_1350; Variance = `VARIANCE(...)`: dw_3311, dw_1350, dw_2151.\n\n### Group B: Term dimension (ACADEMIC_TERMS vs ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL vs ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER)\nACADEMIC_TERMS carries TERM_DESCRIPTION plus status columns; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL is a superset without IS_REGULAR_TERM/TERM_STATUS; ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER holds only 3 relative-term rows. The task needs only TERM_DESCRIPTION and the hint join keys name ACADEMIC_TERMS explicitly → ACADEMIC_TERMS: SUPPORTED; the others: not required by hints (no discriminating need).\n\n### Group C: Material status domains (TIP vs Library)\nPer column_concept_material_status_key comparisons: independent value domains; \"required course materials\" in a TIP-hinted task maps to 'RQ' in TIP_DETAIL only; library 'Y' is excluded (hints list TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, not LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: consumed by dozens of catalog-attribute metrics (dw_3248, dw_3635, dw_2090, dw_1758, dw_2151, dw_104, dw_2597...); serves \"subjects offered in academic year X with N units\" question patterns.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: enriches offerings with TERM_DESCRIPTION / IS_REGULAR_TERM / TERM_STATUS in nearly all subject-offering metrics.\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY**: enrollment/unit statistics by department/term; in the 2024-12-unit prece