y in hint mappings and exact precedent SQL shapes.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Recommended tables/columns:**\n- Main listing: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_NUMBER, SUBJECT_TITLE, DEPARTMENT_NAME, ACADEMIC_YEAR=2024, TOTAL_UNITS=12) joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS on EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE = TERM_CODE for TERM_DESCRIPTION, plus SUBJECT_SUMMARY on TERM_CODE — exactly the join triple used by precedents dw_3248/dw_3635/dw_2090 for the identical wording, and matching all four hint join keys.\n- Rank: `RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY t0.SUBJECT_CODE)`.\n- Department stats: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ TIP_DETAIL ON SUBJECT_ID ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY ON SUBJECT_ID, filtered `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ'` and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 1`, grouped by OFFER_DEPT_NAME, computing `AVG(TOTAL_UNITS)`, `MAX(TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(TOTAL_UNITS)`, `VARIANCE(TOTAL_UNITS)` — the dw_4724 Sub2 join shape with the dw_3311/dw_1350 stat expressions, per the hint column mapping.\n- Attach stats to the listing via LEFT JOIN on DEPARTMENT_NAME = OFFER_DEPT_NAME (same academic value domain per column_concept_department_name; LEFT JOIN keeps all 2024 12-unit subjects even where a department has no qualifying TIP stats).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** two CTEs (subject listing with window rank; per-department stats), LEFT JOIN on department name, ORDER BY DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUBJECT_CODE. No rounding applied. SELECT list contains exactly the 9 requested fields in order: subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, rank, average, range, variance.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the only candidate with ACADEMIC_YEAR + SUBJECT_CODE/SUBJECT_NUMBER + TOTAL_UNITS together (retrieved column definitions); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY is the only stats-side table with both TOTAL_UNITS and a SUBJECT_ID join to TIP_DETAIL (hint join key). Fan-out from TIP_DETAIL's material-level grain is absorbed by the GROUP BY in the stats CTE; the SUBJECT_SUMMARY term-join fan-out in the listing CTE mirrors the accepted precedent shape (dw_3248/dw_3635/dw_2090) and does not affect the RANK expression's partition/order semantics as used in those precedents.\n- **Semantic-network**: column_concept_material_status_key decision_guide anchors \"required\" to TIP 'RQ'; column_concept_total_units decision_guide assigns catalog filtering to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS and rollup-level unit stats to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS; concept_subject_offering_facts documents the shared SUBJECT_ID/TERM_CODE identity across the joined tables.\n- **Business**: four precedent metrics use the verbatim \"academic year 2024 … total of 12 units … rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code\" pattern with the same CTE structure; dw_4724 establishes the TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED→TIP_DETAIL→SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY department-stats pattern with 'RQ'; dw_1350 establishes \"at least one enrolled student\" = `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 1` and the AVG/MAX−MIN/VARIANCE trio.\n\n**6d. Alternatives/tie-breakers:** `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0` (dw_1954 style) is equivalent to `>= 1` for integer counts, so no tie exists. Using SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS instead of SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS for the stats would contradict the explicit hint mapping; the hint is the tie-breaker. The submission was accepted (case dw_3847).\n\n**Final SQL** (submitted): the two-CTE query shown in 6b, returning SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_NUMBER, SUBJECT_TITLE, DEPARTMENT_NAME, TERM_DESCRIPTION, department rank, avg_total_units, range_total_units, variance_total_units, ordered by DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUBJECT_CODE.",
